{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>About midnight.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory have already spoken (Berakhot 4a) regarding the reason it says כַּחֲצוֹת with a כ. And perhaps it further intends, according to the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 43:3) regarding the verse (Genesis 14:15) ״וַיֵּחָלֵק עֲלֵיהֶם לַיְלָה״ — for it was the night of the fifteenth of Nisan. They further said of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 42) that the slaying of the four kings that Abraham killed destroyed several faiths, and it was also a great and mighty battle renowned among the kings of the world, for they were powerful kings who ruled over five great and mighty kings, and one man with his household servants defeated them. Therefore He indicated to him the time and said to him <b>about midnight</b> — the one known in the world, when I went forth to save Abraham their father — likewise ״אֲנִי יוֹצֵא״ etc." "<b>I will go out etc.</b> Meaning: although I have many attendants, nevertheless I Myself will go out in the midst of Egypt. And the reason is twofold: first, because of love for the children, so that their departure would be through Him in His glory and in person. Second, because no angel can make the great distinction regarding who was formed from the first drop of a man, so as to be called a firstborn — even though he is second or third to the womb — except He who forms, He who creates, blessed be He, knows the drops He forms, who and who is the firstborn."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:38.287390127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}